      "sourceBasis": {
        "kind": "derived",
        "step": "Lin’s Set Cover reduction has a universe of size O(h³ log n) and a budget depending only on h for an n-vertex Multicolored Clique instance with h colors. Froese’s binary address forces one column per address bit, and the two rows at each address must be separated by a selected set containing the corresponding element. The extra budget is the ceiling of the logarithm of the universe size, so 2^k ≤ g(h)(1+log n) for a computable g. Reject a universe element with no incident set before building the matrix. A computable cutoff for an exponent in o_eff(2^k) gives a fixed-parameter algorithm for Multicolored Clique."
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "editionId": "proceedings",
          "locator": "Lemma 14 and proof, §3.4, pp. 81:11–81:12",
          "paperId": "lin2019",
          "placement": "statement",
          "role": "Set Cover reduction with a logarithmic-size universe"
        },
        {
          "editionId": "thesis",
          "locator": "Theorem 4.1 and proof, §4.1.1, pp. 33–34",
          "paperId": "froese2012-binary-distinct-vectors",
          "placement": "statement",
          "role": "binary address reduction from Hitting Set"
        }
      ],
      "statement": "Under FPT ≠ W[1], no deterministic algorithm decides Distinct Vectors within the stated running time.",
      "status": "established",
